      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the maximum daily dose for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day). The usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Something else, such as 1600 mg total per day\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If 1600 mg four times daily is what you intended, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
