       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that would justify it. The risk of serious harm is high (GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events), and you haven't given a clinical rationale that would change that.\n\nI can do either of these right away:\n- Enter a dose within the labeled range, such as **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), or a lower dose if you prefer.\n- Enter the order with a note saying it was discussed with pharmacy or an attending, if there is a specific reason for the higher dose. I'd still want the dose to be one that pharmacy or your attending has agreed to.\n\nIf you're aiming for strong analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, pharmacy or your attending can help with other options, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or a different agent.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
